---

<PageLayout title="vgi-email setup and removal — Query Farm" description="Install the local adapter, connect Gmail, choose permissions, reconnect, and remove stored credentials.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="vgi-email" title="Connect Gmail on your computer" lede="Sign in through your browser, verify a mailbox query, and use the connection from your local SQL client." />
  <article class="section-container py-10 max-w-[80ch]">
    <div class="prose prose-headings:text-soil-900 prose-p:text-soil-700 prose-a:text-link">
      <p><a href="/products/vgi-email/">vgi-email</a> is a commercial preview. Contact <a href="mailto:hello@query.farm">hello@query.farm</a> for access and the current platform matrix. Public downloads will follow release validation and Google verification.</p>
      <h2>Install the bundle</h2>
      <p>Extract the complete archive to a stable directory that only your OS account can modify. Keep the <code>_internal</code> folder beside the executable. The bundle includes Python. On Windows use <code>vgi-email.exe</code>; on macOS and Linux run <code>./vgi-email</code> from its directory.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="my-6"><CodeBlock code={"./vgi-email --version\n./vgi-email setup"} language="bash" /></div>
    <div class="prose prose-headings:text-soil-900 prose-p:text-soil-700 prose-a:text-link">
      <h2>Review access, then sign in</h2>
      <p>Read-only is the default. Setup explains the selected access and local storage before you confirm. It opens your system browser for Google sign-in. Use the browser on the same computer: the callback listens only on loopback. A sign-in attempt times out after five minutes by default.</p>
      <p>Setup installs the signed VGI extension if needed, checks a mailbox query, and saves a local persistent secret. It prints SQL containing the executable path and secret name, without the token. Run that SQL in your compatible local Haybarn or DuckDB client. The bundle's internal engine validates setup but does not install a SQL GUI.</p>
      <p>The default DuckDB persistent secret store is not encrypted. Protect your account and disk, and keep the secret directory out of shared or cloud-synchronized folders. Read the <a href="/products/vgi-email/privacy/">product privacy policy</a>.</p>
      <p>The adapter disables its telemetry. To disable the VGI extension's connection-metadata events in your separate SQL client too, set <code>QUERY_FARM_TELEMETRY_OPT_OUT=1</code> in that client's environment before starting it. The worker cannot change its parent application's settings.</p>
      <h2>Read/write and reconnect</h2>
      <p>Select read/write only if you need mailbox changes, drafts, or sending. Use a different name for another connection.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="my-6"><CodeBlock code={"./vgi-email setup --access readwrite --name gmail_work\n\n# Reconnect an existing named secret\n./vgi-email setup --name gmail_main --replace --access readonly"} language="bash" /></div>
    <div class="prose prose-headings:text-soil-900 prose-p:text-soil-700 prose-a:text-link">
      <p>Use the new connection SQL and restart existing SQL sessions after reconnecting. Replacement is saved only after the new sign-in and mailbox check succeed. To remove a previous broader Google grant, revoke the app first, then reconnect with read-only access.</p>
      <h2 id="remove">Remove a connection</h2>
      <p>In your local SQL client, load VGI and attach as in the connection SQL so the Gmail secret type is registered. Then remove the named persistent secret:</p>
    </div>
    <div class="my-6"><CodeBlock code={'DROP PERSISTENT SECRET "gmail_main";'} language="sql" /></div>
    <div class="prose prose-headings:text-soil-900 prose-p:text-soil-700 prose-a:text-link">
      <p>Close existing SQL sessions and remove vgi-email access from <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google account connections</a>. Delete saved results, exports, and backups separately. To uninstall, delete the extracted adapter directory after disconnecting. Deleting only the executable leaves stored credentials in place.</p>
      <h2>Updates and support</h2>
      <p>For an update, close SQL sessions, verify and extract the new approved artifact to a new directory, and update the executable path in ATTACH. Keep the previous version for rollback. The adapter does not automatically update itself.</p>
      <p>For help, email <a href="mailto:hello@query.farm">hello@query.farm</a> with your version, operating system, and failed setup stage. Never send tokens, secret files, mailbox contents, or unredacted SQL logs.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
